WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.234
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:04.529 --> 00:00:06.070
SPEAKER 1: This
Quick Start shows you

00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:10.000
how to perform basic operations
in Datastore using the Google

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.380
Cloud Platform Console.

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:15.170
Go to the Datastore Entities
page in the Google Cloud

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:16.940
Platform Console.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:20.840
This page allows you to store,
query, update, and delete data.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:23.100
Click Create Entity.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:27.080
On the Create Entity page, use
Default for Namespace and Task

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:28.940
for Kind.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:31.690
Under Properties, use
the Add Property button

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:33.710
to add the following
properties--

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:37.910
a description of type String
whose value is Learn Google

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:40.510
Cloud Datastore.

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:43.420
Click Done to set the property.

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:47.780
Use the Add Property button to
add a second property, named

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:52.640
Created, with the Type Date and
Time, with the current time.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:54.710
Click Done to set
this [? property. ?]

00:00:54.710 --> 00:01:01.090
Now let's add a third property,
called Done, of type Boolean,

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:03.700
with a value of False.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:08.850
Click Done to set the
property, and click Create.

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:12.920
And note that the console
now displays the task entity

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:14.580
that you just created.

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:17.342
You just stored data
in Cloud Datastore.

00:01:17.342 --> 00:01:19.800
Now that our Datastore is up
and running, let's run a query

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:22.650
and click on Query by GQL.

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:26.280
Enter "Select, star,
from task" as the query.

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:28.830
Note that "task"
is case-sensitive.

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:31.500
When we click Run
Query, we can see

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:35.670
that the results show the
task entity we just created.

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:38.460
You can add a query filter
to restrict the results

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:41.180
to entities that meet
specific criteria.

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:43.380
Let's run a query
such as "Select, star,

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:47.970
from task where done equals
false," and click Run Query.

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:50.100
Note that "done"
is case-sensitive.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:53.400
And the results show the task
entity that you just created,

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:56.880
since its done value is false.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:58.140
Congratulations.

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:03.150
You've just stored and queried
data in Cloud Datastore.

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:06.500
[MUSIC PLAYING]

